        ],
        "text": "Oral argument began at 11:19\u202fa.m."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e1910c5fd31d-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Chief Justice Roberts asked whether a state law requiring disclosure of any potential conflict of interest would cause a person to lose the case."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e1910c5fd31d-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kennedy, justice Kennedy inquired about the federal balance of the case."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e1910c5fd31d-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Stevens asked whether the prohibited action\u2014voting\u2014must be contrary to the interest of the other party."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e1910c5fd31d-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 40,
              "start": 40
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, justice Breyer presented a hypothetical about a person sabotaging his employer\u2019s meeting."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e1910c5fd31d-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 42,
              "start": 42
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, justice Scalia questioned why Congress did not use clearer language."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e1910c5fd31d-0002-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 54,
              "start": 54
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Stevens asked whether a violation is complete only if the official votes in the interest of the company rather than the polls."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e1910c5fd31d-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 59,
              "start": 59
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Stevens asked whether the party would win on the facts rather than the legal theory."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
